1. She is excited about attending V Expo in Birmingham, England, where she will participate in two panels and a meet and greet. (Verbatim: "I'm going to be doing two panels and a meet and greet.")
2. She identifies as being from England. (Verbatim: "I live in England, it's grim all the time, so...")
3. She has a strong emotional reaction to losing in Teamfight Tactics, describing herself as feeling "eliminated" and emotionally drained. (Verbatim: "I just felt like, eliminated, it's me, what up, the eliminated girl from the TFT tournament.")
4. She has a very addictive personality, particularly when it comes to gaming. (Verbatim: "I have a very addictive personality. Like, very, very, very.")
5. She plays Teamfight Tactics obsessively, sometimes to the point of forgetting to eat and losing sleep. (Verbatim: "I tried to lock in and play teamfight tactics the whole day. The whole day. And I did not do well. And I forgot to eat.")
6. She has played Danganronpa and 999, both visual novels with puzzle elements, and remembers them fondly despite playing them years after release. (Verbatim: "I played 999, it's not a very big game, it was on like... What did I play it on? I can't even remember.")
7. She is currently in the beta for a new game called Tribe 9, created by the same developer behind 999 and Danganronpa. (Verbatim: "I got into the beta for it, I need to find out if I'm allowed to stream it...")
8. She has a tendency to stay awake for extended periods to finish visual novels, prioritizing story completion over sleep. (Verbatim: "I had friends messaging like, yo, Elliot, you've been online for like over 20 hours straight playing this game, are you okay?")
9. She is emotionally invested in games, describing a specific feeling of being fueled to try again despite knowing it's a bad idea. (Verbatim: "You know you're not in the right mindset. You know this is a terrible, terrible, terrible idea. But, but you are fueled.")
10. She describes herself as stubborn, especially when it comes to not wanting to give up in games, even when under-leveled or struggling. (Verbatim: "I'm stubborn. You guys have seen, I'm like, I'm like a very, very stubborn person.") [end of text]



1. She initially applied to study medicine but dropped out before starting due to lack of motivation. (Verbatim: "I dropped out before before the first before i even started because i just knew i just knew i was like this is gonna be so much effort")
2. She switched from medicine to a biology-related course after being accepted into the same university. (Verbatim: "i still want to go to your university but could i do this course instead")
3. She considered dentistry as an alternative path because its first year is identical to medicine's, allowing for a potential transfer. (Verbatim: "what something a lot of sneaky people used to do would be apply for dentistry because it's less competitive do the first year which is exactly the same")
4. She pursued a master's degree in computer science after initially studying biology. (Verbatim: "when i went to do my master's and then i was going to go to do my doctorate to continue the work my master's thesis was in")
5. She decided against pursuing a PhD because she lacked passion for the subject and felt it would be a waste of a competitive funding slot. (Verbatim: "i thought it's just a wasted slot if it was like wasted on this punk and that punk being me")
6. She chose to become a VTuber because it is something she can passionately and happily dedicate herself to full-time. (Verbatim: "vtubing is that for sure you know and when it comes to like yeah i would never what you call it")
7. She worked in data entry for a short time and found it initially fun due to treating it like a game, but it became mind-numbing over time. (Verbatim: "i was just having fun trying to like give myself a new high score i treated it like a game because it was and it made me really fast with the number pad")
8. She had a negative experience working for a company where the head could not use a computer properly and was promoted despite incompetence. (Verbatim: "the head of it couldn't use a computer i was like why is this punk the head of it getting paid more than double everyone else here he literally can't use a keyboard properly")
9. She was offered multiple raises when trying to quit her job, which she found frustrating and indicative of being trapped. (Verbatim: "every time i said i wanted to quit the company was like but what if we gave you more money and i was like you think i can be bought you're right damn it")
10. She was at risk of being expelled from college due to poor attendance but was allowed to stay because her grades were strong. (Verbatim: "technically based on my attendance i should have been expelled because i wasn't there half the time") [end of text]



1. She has a bachelor's degree in animal biology and a master's degree in computer science. (Verbatim: "my bachelor's was like um animal biology and then my master's was computer science")
2. She has worked multiple jobs simultaneously to support family finances. (Verbatim: "i did have to work a lot of jobs like simultaneously to like help with family finances and stuff")
3. She has experience in software development, database architecture, data entry, administration, data science, and lab science. (Verbatim: "i've done like first second third line support i've done like a software developer um i've done database architecture work i've done data entry i've done administration work i've done i am a fully trained data scientist i'm also a fully trained lab scientist")
4. She dislikes database administration work due to its complexity and lack of clear schema. (Verbatim: "i really dislike dba work there's never the right schema for the day")
5. She finds SQL (referred to as "sequel") easy to learn and recommends it for beginners. (Verbatim: "sequel is really nice to pick up it's really easy to pick up")
6. She identifies as a cat person and was raised by a cat. (Verbatim: "i'm almost convinced i'm not a goose i'm a cat i was basically raised by my cat")
7. She misses her childhood cat and often slept with it. (Verbatim: "my cat would always sleep in my bed with me growing up okay so i grew up with a cat that i love very much that i miss")
8. She struggles with self-doubt and anxiety despite appearing positive. (Verbatim: "i know i come across as a positive person i'm not i'm a very negative person so you know like i'm the kind of person that's got a head full of self-doubt all the time")
9. She has a strong ambition to make a big difference in the world. (Verbatim: "i want to be able to make a big big big difference like big difference in the world")
10. She believes that the key to programming is knowing how to effectively use search engines. (Verbatim: "every developer is just really good at googling stuff like that's it that's it") [end of text]



1. She has a deep emotional bond with her late cat, which would sit on her head while she slept. (Verbatim: "imagine like the side of my head that's like facing upwards my cat would just sit there... just sit on my head like that and that was one of the spots my cat liked to just sit and like i guess protect me or something")
2. Her cat was very affectionate only at night and would follow her to every room, staying in view but not close. (Verbatim: "my cat would just follow me to every room which is funny because like even if my cat wasn't feeling very cuddly... it would just follow me and wouldn't sit with me but like sit like in view of me and just be there")
3. Her cat was standoffish with others but extremely loving toward her, making the bond feel special. (Verbatim: "this cat was not friendly with other people... but it was so loving towards me so it felt like extra extra special")
4. She misses her cat deeply and has a strong affection for cats in general. (Verbatim: "i miss my cat i miss my cat i love cats")
5. She has a habit of sleeping on her side and often lies down in that position after streams. (Verbatim: "i normally sleep on my side okay so imagine i'm sat on my side sat on my side lying down on my side now")
6. She once sacrificed tournament time to fix her sleeping pattern for the Expo. (Verbatim: "I decided to sleep between like like the night time is like right before and I could have I could have just played and then not lost that one life")
7. She has a strong emotional connection to gaming, particularly Teamfight Tactics, and views it as a significant part of her identity. (Verbatim: "always sacrifice myself for team fight tactics always it is the way it is the way")
8. She once attempted to "lock in" during a stream but failed due to lack of chat support. (Verbatim: "i didn't stream and actually actually tried to lock in that's what i get for trying")
9. She has a self-deprecating sense of humor about her stream habits, joking about being "yapped" off the stream. (Verbatim: "how did i get eliminated was i yapping too much yes yes let's blame it on the yap")
10. She has a desire to do a karaoke stream in the future, indicating a personal aspiration related to performance. (Verbatim: "i really need to do a karaoke stream one day") [end of text]



1. She worked at a zoo handling various animals, including rhinos, zebras, donkeys, and birds. (Verbatim: "i used to be able to lift a lot better i did have to do a lot of like lifting work so like um one of the things they don't tell you um is when you work at the zoo there's a lot of lifting")
2. She found the physical demands of zoo work, particularly lifting heavy food bags and bales, to be exhausting. (Verbatim: "those those like the food pellets those those are like 30 kilo bags and um it sucks it sucks like yeah having to carry a 30 kilo food bag")
3. She struggled with being assertive, especially when handling animals like donkeys and during falconry. (Verbatim: "i'm not very good at being very assertive um it was definitely the thing i struggled most with when it came to like uh falconry")
4. She had to walk a hand-reared cow that would run away from new staff members. (Verbatim: "there was one cow that was hand-reared okay the hand-reared cow wasn't afraid to mess with people and every time someone new joined it would be their first task to walk this one hecking cow")
5. She found falconry difficult due to her naturally non-demanding demeanor. (Verbatim: "i'm not one to sound very demanding so like if you're asking a bird to go from a to b you have to be like here i'm like i'm british right i'm gonna be like yo bird would you like to come over")
6. She cared for a pair of rhinos with distinct personalities—one gentle and one prone to violent outbursts every few days. (Verbatim: "there were two rhinos i looked after one was really gentle and pretty chill the other one woke up and decided to choose violence every two or three days")
7. She enjoyed the unique personalities of the animals she worked with, finding them interesting and endearing. (Verbatim: "one thing one thing that i found great was like working with all the different animals and learning all their different personalities")
8. She found the interaction with rhinos, especially giving them scritches, to be a positive experience. (Verbatim: "i could give the rhino scritches if it wasn't a happy mood but because like rhinos have the rhinos have the the thing where they feel happiness from pets")
9. She has a fondness for British English expressions and enjoys reading them in chat. (Verbatim: "i do actually love reading when people write in british in chat and i like to just read it out loud")
10. She has a playful, self-aware sense of humor about her lack of physical strength and her "spaghetti arms." (Verbatim: "i'm happy with my spaghetti arms i'll be honest like yeah i'm happy with my spaghetti arms") [end of text]



1. She has a history of agoraphobia, which was medically diagnosed and treated with therapy. (Verbatim: "for those that don't know i had i had agoraphobia um like proper like you know proper medically diagnosed got given therapy for in all sorts")
2. She experiences anxiety in crowded or public environments due to a lack of perceived control. (Verbatim: "it's like the fear of crowds or technically it's more of like the fear of being in an environment where you lack the control of like and yeah and um yeah outside is that so it doesn't necessarily have to be crowded")
3. She finds large gatherings of people overwhelming and has an instinctive reaction to avoid them. (Verbatim: "i'm a lot better now though like a lot better i still have an like you know instinctive reaction of oh my god i'd rather take the route less taken because there's less people on it and i'm scared of people")
4. She once had a distressing experience while walking with her dog, where she was accidentally bumped into by someone and felt helpless due to the lack of fast travel options in real life. (Verbatim: "i did a walk with my dog once and i made the mistake because irl doesn't have fast travel return um so i did this ridiculously long hike and i was so far away from home and it started raining and i was so sad")
5. She enjoys playing Teamfight Tactics (TFT), a strategy game, and continues to play it even outside of tournaments. (Verbatim: "i still want to climb and stuff i do enjoy tft it is a game that i i do very much love so like yeah yeah yeah yeah yeah")
6. She struggles with decision-making, particularly in high-pressure situations like in TFT. (Verbatim: "my biggest issue in teamfight tactics is that there's so many decisions you have to make and I'm not one to make decisions I just don't want to get in trouble")
7. She has a soft spot for quiet ASMR streams and has considered doing them again, though she is cautious about copyright. (Verbatim: "I've not done ASMR for a while mostly because I've just been trying to fit in what I can but yeah yeah for sure I have my I have my ASMR mic now that I'm back at home")
8. She values the emotional support she receives from her viewers, which helps her manage her mental health. (Verbatim: "streaming has helped me um you guys definitely support me mentally very very very much for sure")
9. She has a strong emotional reaction to being treated unfairly in public, such as being blamed for an accident caused by someone else. (Verbatim: "she wasn't me i think they were they were they acted like it was all my fault and i was kind of sad because i didn't do anything")
10. She has a deep appreciation for the structure and routine of her sleep schedule, which she has worked to maintain. (Verbatim: "well i fixed my sleeping pattern we're not letting that sacrifice go to waste now are we") [end of text]



1. She is a VTuber who performs under the name Elia Stellaria. (Verbatim: "i'm a vtuber so i believe the etiquette is to to not know who i am")
